From f114d3e0ae60c1fb947d55a98d7a03947eddbaaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: isoriano1968 <isoriano1968@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:58:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 37/42] config/amix/include: more SVR4.0 gaps; amix.cf: no
 libiaf

New wrappers (CDE-owned, #include_next the AMIX header where there is one):
- iostream.h, fstream.h, strstream.h: the pre-standard C++ headers as the
  standard ones with their names in the global namespace;
- strings.h: <string.h> plus strcasecmp/strncasecmp (libamixc99);
- iconv.h: stand-in whose iconv_open always fails (C locale only);
- nl_types.h: NL_CAT_LOCALE (0, the XPG3 behaviour);
- unistd.h: seteuid/setegid (libc) and rresvport (libsocket) declared;
- sys/mman.h: munmap/mprotect/msync declared, madvise via memcntl;
- sys/uio.h: readv/writev declared;
- sys/systeminfo.h: SYS_NMLN from <sys/utsname.h> first.
Changed: sys/stat.h declares fchmod; wchar.h makes putwc/getwc functions
(callers #undef getwc to get "the libc function").

EUSCompat.h: the AMIX section takes MAXNAMELEN from <sys/param.h> and
iconv from the stand-in instead of its own macros.
amix.cf: IafSysLib empty -- libiaf is SVR4.2, dtlogin links without it.
